#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:14
msgid "Product capabilities described by the assets"
msgstr "Capacitats del producte descrites pels recursos"

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:16
msgid ""
"The harness content defines a proposed LLM-operated tax-advisory workflow"
" around Cadrumo’s deterministic CLI/MCP interfaces. Seven personas divide"
" responsibilities: onboarding, ledger grooming, classification, modelo "
"preparation, independent verification, coordination, and post-filing "
"reconciliation. The intended sequence is to establish a profile and read "
"access, build and classify source-faithful books, prepare a registry-"
"selected declaration, independently verify it, export a local artefact, "
"have the taxpayer file outside the product, then reconcile against "
"official evidence (role definitions "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/personas/cadrumo-coordinator.md`), "
"independent verifier (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/personas/cadrumo-"
"verifier.md`), human filing handoff "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules/cadrumo-operator-safety-"
"handoff.md`)). The bookkeeper is instructed to preserve transaction "
"provenance and use idempotency keys for safe add retries; the classifier "
"assigns tax categories and ratios but does not compute tax; the preparer "
"reads calculated revisions and cannot self-verify."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:18
msgid ""
"Seven operator-rule documents establish the proposed safety contract: "
"read structured response envelopes, retain receipts and unresolved IDs, "
"use currently exposed MCP operations rather than infer tool availability "
"from CLI spellings, preserve `legal_refs` and `source_refs`, surface "
"warnings and actionable verdicts, never compute values from memory, and "
"never treat a local export as official filing evidence (envelope and "
"recovery handling (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules/cadrumo-"
"operator-envelope-reading.md`), operating rules "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules/cadrumo-operator-operating-"
"rules.md`), lifecycle ordering (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules"
"/cadrumo-operator-lifecycle-ordering.md`)). The coordinator is asked to "
"dispatch verification with tool-result JSON alone, and the verifier must "
"look for positive-input/zero-tax under-declaration shapes rather than "
"accept an empty clean result without question (independent context "
"requirement (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/personas/cadrumo-"
"verifier.md`), honest-declaration rule "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules/cadrumo-operator-honest-"
"declaration.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:20
msgid ""
"The assigned workflow skills cover onboarding, rental income, both "
"individual-business regimes, activity start/cessation, quarter close, "
"intra-community transactions, ledger upkeep, classification, export, and "
"model-specific preparation for 100, 111, 115, 130, 131, 180, 190, 193, "
"200, 202, and 303. YAML frontmatter supplies routing hints such as "
"profile facts, workflow phases, and temporal triggers; the prose gives "
"preconditions, command sequences, success checks, and handoffs. The "
"repeated operational pattern is inspect applicability and form shape from"
" the CLI, create/calculate/read the revision, surface notices and "
"provenance, verify independently, export only after the gate, and "
"reconcile only after the human files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:22
msgid ""
"Several guides give a useful provenance map rather than treating all "
"inputs alike. Modelo 100 distinguishes ledger-derived activity income "
"from profile facts and manually entered non-business income; Modelo 131 "
"says objective-estimation figures come from the taxpayer’s own worksheet "
"while the ledger remains relevant for IVA/evidence; Modelo 200 identifies"
" manual accounting-result inputs, profile-based entity/INCN facts, and "
"Modelo 202 credits (Modelo 100 orientation "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-100/reference/casillas.md`), Modelo 131 orientation "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-131/reference/casillas.md`), Modelo 200 guide "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-200/SKILL.md`)). Annual withholding forms document quarterly "
"relation fold-ins and distinguish computed totals from row-level data. "
"The Modelo 180 guidance explicitly warns that per-landlord rows are "
"manual and not checked merely because calculation succeeds; the Modelo "
"190 and 193 guides describe registry-specific annual rollups (Modelo 180 "
"detail warning (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-180/reference/casillas.md`), Modelo 190 annual workflow "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-190/SKILL.md`), Modelo 193 guide "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-193/SKILL.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:24
msgid "Knowledge and data"
msgstr "Coneixement i dades"

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:26
msgid ""
"The content repeatedly names the registry and actual tool results as the "
"authority for form revisions, casillas, formulas, deadlines, "
"applicability, and provenance. The casilla companions identify themselves"
" as orientation only and tell operators to query the exact year/period "
"rather than report values from prose. Skills also carry detailed legal "
"references, revision-specific examples, and asserted formula behavior. "
"These statements describe the snapshot’s intended knowledge and must not "
"be represented as independently verified current law; some are explicitly"
" year-specific (for example the Modelo 131 2025 cross-check and the "
"Modelo 190/193 revision transitions). The orientation rule itself directs"
" legal questions to governing official sources (registry grounding "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules/cadrumo-operator-grounding.md`), "
"casilla orientation limitation (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills"
"/cadrumo-preparar-modelo-130/reference/casillas.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:28
msgid "Security and implementation assessment"
msgstr "Avaluació de seguretat i implementació"

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:30
msgid ""
"The strongest safety properties are expressed as instructions, not "
"enforced here. The material says role assignment grants no authority, "
"requires checking the bound profile and current registered-operation "
"contract, calls for separate agent sessions, keeps API secrets in "
"protected storage, restricts scratch-file/external-service use, requires "
"human confirmation for destructive acts, and forbids live AEAT submission"
" (operator authority boundaries (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules"
"/cadrumo-operator-operating-rules.md`), storage and AEAT boundary "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules/cadrumo-operator-safety-"
"handoff.md`)). These are meaningful guardrails for an LLM workflow, but "
"the assigned code is only an inert namespace plus text; it does not "
"verify current grants, enforce tool schemas, isolate sessions, protect "
"secrets, block actions, or check that the verifier received independent "
"context. Actual enforcement depends on the harness loader, runtime tool "
"adapter, operation authorization, and application gates outside this "
"chunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:32
msgid ""
"The content identifies a particularly important documented gap: Modelo "
"202 casilla 33 (minimum payment for large taxpayers) is described as "
"manual with no formula, binding, or verification guard, so the agent is "
"told to ask explicitly when INCN reaches the stated threshold (Modelo 202"
" gap and operator check (`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-"
"preparar-modelo-202/reference/casillas.md`), Modelo 202 procedure "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/skills/cadrumo-preparar-"
"modelo-202/SKILL.md`)). This is a prompt-level mitigation for a claimed "
"product gap, not an enforced validator. Other under-declaration checks "
"likewise depend on notices or operator reasoning; an instruction to stop "
"does not itself prevent export."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:34
msgid ""
"There is a useful interface warning but also an integration dependency: "
"the operator rules say a CLI path does not establish MCP exposure or "
"permission, while many skills present concrete CLI command recipes. Safe "
"use through MCP therefore depends on the runtime mapping each requested "
"task to the currently discovered and described operation, and refusing if"
" absent. The skills cannot themselves prove this mapping or enforce that "
"a human authorized a state change. Likewise, “independent verifier” "
"depends on invocation isolation and actual result-only context "
"construction, not the persona text (MCP/CLI distinction "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/rules/cadrumo-operator-envelope-"
"reading.md`), verifier trust caveat "
"(`src/cadrumo_harness/_data/agent/personas/cadrumo-verifier.md`))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/articles/186-agent-personas-operator-rules-and-workflow-skills.md:36
msgid ""
"No conventional software defect is established in this documentation-only"
" chunk. The main unresolved questions are whether the frontmatter schema "
"is parsed and validated, how personas/rules/skills are selected and "
"composed, whether all claimed workflow names resolve to current "
"operations, how prompt injection and tool-result content are bounded, and"
" which actions have application-level gates. No tests, current legal "
"verification, deployment behavior, or runtime enforcement were inspected."
msgstr ""

